The supplier shall develop and document, for each requirement of the software item in RB, including IRD, a set of tests, test cases and test procedures including:
testing against the mission data and scenario specified by the customer in 5.2.3.1;
testing with stress, boundary, and singular inputs;
testing the software product for its ability to isolate and reduce the effect of errors;
testing that the software product can perform successfully in a representative operational and non-intrusive environment;
external interface testing including boundaries, protocols and timing test;
testing HMI applications as per ECSS-E-ST-10-11;
security testing against security requirements as per clause 5.2.2.1.
EXPECTED OUTPUT: Software validation specification with respect to the requirements baseline [DJF, SVS; QR, AR].
NOTE 1 A test case identifies inputs, outputs, and test criteria.
NOTE 2 The reduction of the effect of an error can be done by graceful degradation upon failure, request for operator assistance upon stress, boundary and singular conditions.
